        plan("The urban livelihoods mission and its components", [3], "The urban mission and the similarly branded rural mission belong to different ministries.", "Name the mission, the ministry and the component before evaluating livelihood support."),
        plan("The shelter component and the norm that measures it", [4], "A provision norm measures facilities planned rather than homeless persons served.", "Separate a coverage norm from evidence that the facility is located where it is used."),
        plan("Where shelter provision actually breaks down", [5], "Land, matching finance and service linkage fail separately and need separate corrections.", "Locate a delivery failure at a named input rather than asserting weak implementation."),
        plan("Vendor credit and its escalating tranches", [6], "These are loans with a subsidy and an incentive, not grants and not a right to vend.", "State a credit instrument by its terms and its repayment condition before assessing reach."),
        plan("The vending statute and the rights it creates", [7], "Credit does not supply the legal livelihood layer that the statute supplies.", "Match the instrument to the harm: eviction is answered by law, not by working capital."),
        plan("The eligibility condition the scheme's own portal records", [8], "Statutory notification by the State is a precondition for the credit route, not a parallel track.", "Cite an official eligibility condition for exactly what it says and no further."),
        plan("Housing sanction and food portability as two realisation tests", [9, 10], "A sanction is not an occupied house, and portability is a mechanism within an existing entitlement.", "Test an entitlement against the moment of realisation rather than the moment of approval."),
        plan("The migrant's legal route and the friction in portability", [11, 12], "Central commencement is not enforcement, and authentication failure blocks a valid entitlement.", "Separate a commenced statute from State rules and from what happens at the counter."),
        plan("The slum scale anchor and the population it misses", [13], "The recorded count excludes informal renters, homeless persons and unnotified settlements.", "Cite a census figure with its year and its recorded exclusions attached."),
        plan("Circular movement against fixed-place entitlement design", [14], "A place-attached entitlement fails a person attached to a circuit, however well funded it is.", "Match the unit of entitlement to the actual pattern of the worker's movement."),
        plan("Why metropolitan pull is structural rather than accidental", [15], "Agglomeration and informal-work availability explain the pattern; blaming the destination does not.", "Explain a migration pattern through push, pull and density before prescribing policy."),
        plan("Area-based development, upgrading and tenure trade-offs", [16, 17], "Area selection can exclude the poorest, and neither upgrading nor resettlement is first-best.", "Argue a spatial policy through its selection rule and its distributional consequence."),
        plan("Who pays, who implements and what is not claimed", [18, 19], "The State matching share and local-body capacity decide delivery, and no routed demand is claimed here.", "Close with a graded verdict, a named institutional correction and an explicit ownership statement."),
